    "title": "Woman rescued from overturned vehicle - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff Writer ,\n5 hours ago\nKEY LARGO — A Florida Fish and Wildlife Conservation Commission (FWC) officer rescued a severely injured woman trapped inside an overturned sedan on Wednesday, Aug. 20.\nFWC Officer Chris Lejarzar was traveling south on U.S. 1 near mile marker 109 at 3:20 p.m. when he responded to a single-vehicle accident. The overturned car was leaking fuel and beginning to restart on its own.\nFearing a fire and finding the vehicle doors inaccessible, Lejarzar began attempts to free the woman. Squeezing through the broken rear windshield, he removed part of the backseat and cut the woman's seatbelt.\nAdditional help soon arrived, and together with Key Largo Volunteer Fire Department, the Florida Highway Patrol and the Monroe County Sheriff’s Office, Lejarzar secured the vehicle and safely extracted the woman while firefighters stopped the fuel leak.\n“I commend Officer Lejarzar and our Monroe County partners for their swift and courageous response,” said Lt.Col. Alfredo Escanio, FWC South Region deputy director. “Their actions demonstrate their bravery and dedication to protecting the community.”\nThe woman was transported to a local hospital for treatment.",
